  "term": "asemia",
  "definition": "Asemia, or asemasia, is a broad historical term for losing the ability to produce or understand signs and symbols, including words, gestures, and other expressive acts. It extends the idea of aphasia beyond speech alone to any learned system used to convey thought or feeling.",
